{
  "description": "Shared conformance vectors for the pipeline expression language. Executed by BOTH the Python suite (tests/pipelines/expressions/test_expression_vectors.py) and the TypeScript suite (frontend/src/lib/expressions/__tests__/vectors.test.ts) so the two implementations cannot drift. An `item`-typed env entry carries an ItemValue's fields (its `metadata` as `{\"data\": {...}}`), whose members are the per-item facts a routing predicate reads; a `metadata` member access is open-keyed and types `string`, with an absent key reading as the empty string. A case may carry an optional `self` map (same entry shape as `env`) naming the config fields of the node the expression sits on, reachable as `self.<field>`; omitted, `self` is unavailable. Each case: parse `source`; if error=syntax expect a syntax error; else type-check against env types (error=type expects failure, otherwise the result type must equal expect.type); then evaluate against env values (error=eval expects failure, otherwise the value must equal expect.value; numbers compare with 1e-9 tolerance).",
